Z||000000||EdsB52||10-30-2001||11:02 AM||||Just like last time we had the blow up, Cliff alienates objectivity, ignores the fact that many people are voluntarily engaging in disputes, and makes me the scapegoat. Why Cliff, is it just easier that way? Last time you not only allowed the cowards to cast idle threats, you lead the cheer; do you call that objectivity? This is a civil post, don't reply with some garbage about removing me or rally all the members against me, because as you well know, I don't care about either. I'm a good guy, but I'm not a cheerleader. Just because you're the moderator doesn't absolve you of the responsibility of being objective. You can abuse that power and rally everyone behind you because this is such a good forum that people will agree with everything you write. Again, cheerleaders. I lost a few people that were on my side a little while ago when I gave my interpretation of religion and Christianity in America. But those people didn't possess the ability to argue against my point, just be angry because they can't. So they avoid argument and assume a position of undefined disdain for me, sounds like the definition of acquiescence. I've never been involved with a group that uses the criterion of siding with whom they like, as opposed to whom they actually agree as I've seen here. Members will defame me for disagreeing with people in this forum that I like and consider that a negative attribute. That's pathetic; in fact it's simple partisan following when you agree with a side as opposed to the merit of an issue. I've peacefully challenged people to various issues in this forum and received very little constructive argumentation. I have a question for everyone; when you look at a thread or a post within a thread, do you look at the writer’s moniker or the text first? That rhetorical question will yield the already given answer that you look at the author and derive preconceptions as you read the post. Proof of that resides in the history of people that have agreed with me and apologized for it. Then you wonder why I slam people in here? Hey, if I'm going to correspond with a bunch of halfwits, I might as well have fun. That doesn't describe all of the members, but many. Without mentioning names, there are a few members that can carry their own in an argument, the rest just angrily spout off.<P>So Cliff, do what you want with this and I don't care that you closed the thread, but for the sake of your dignity try not to resort to a call for the cheerleaders to unite.||||reg||1
