Z||000002||buds||10-30-2001||11:14 AM||||This would be a much nicer place to hang out with out eds always shootin his trap off..<P>Please vote in my poll: ban or not<P>BAN his sorry ass||||reg||13
Z||000003||stimpy||10-30-2001||11:22 AM||||Ed, while I like to call em as I see em, I generally try not to get into disagreements with you. I don't always agree or disagree with your viewpoints, but I often take issue with your methods. In the case that you are currently bringing up, I actually agree that posting a picture of a significant other in order to solicit "ratings" on her is a pathetic cry for acknowledgement. My wife would smother me in my sleep if I pulled crap like that. It was, in my opine, a very immature thing to do. That being said, who the hell really cares? Does it change the quality of your lifestyle if dude wants to turn a thread into a high school slam book? <P>Sticking with the whole "cheerleader" sports metaphor, I would say that you enjoy taking the role of "instigator". I do think you take some pleasure at getting folks riled and against you. It's all pretty entertaining, like a fight in hockey.  But just like a fight in hockey, eventually it's gotta get broken up and penalties need to be called. So now, on your way to the box, you gotta head-butt the ref (Cliff). And you wonder why you are seen as a "villain". Hmmm.<P>I don't suggest that you leave, in fact, I would be pretty alienated to the whole forum thing here if you were to be the first person "banished" for having legitamate viewpoints that are unpopular. God knows, I've been in that position several times myself. I don't neccesarily suggest that you censor yourself either. I think we should all have the right to say what's on our mind. However, I do believe that the vast majority of the members of the forum would prefer not to have these incessant pissing contests. Eventually Cliff will stop in and close a thread as is his right. Stop looking so shocked when he does.||||reg||6
