Z||000020||Voytek||10-30-2001||01:25 PM||||While the 'host-bashing' issue that some of you are raising is valid, I believe Cliff had more reasons for banning Ed.  After all, Cliff's been insulted before (see the 'Cliff is the same person as Archie' thread - or something along those lines - sorry I don't feel like looking for it).<P>Most of us can take a beating and defend ourselves.  What we've had here is a someone who showed a great deal of disrespect to others.  The word 'instigator' doesn't do him justice.<P>In the above mentioned thread, some vowed that they will never again reply to Ed.  Of course, it's generally in human nature to defend our beliefs so it became hard to leave alone unwarranted comments.  On the other hand, some didn't mind Ed's little stunts (or perhaps didn't see what put him on the black list)and continued to post replies and make him feel as welcome as anyone.  Perhaps, had we all ignored him completely, maybe he'd have chosen to go somewhere else.<P>While many of us enjoy a good debate, the phrase 'healthy debate' has all but disappeared from any thread contributed to by Ed.  Maybe he had some personal reasons for doing this; after all, he did get quite a few people worked up (including myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> )and turned a number of threads into complete trash.<P>I've had disagreements with members and their comments in the past but have never seen so much garbage come from one keyboard.<P>I hope PFF doesn't have to go through this again.||||reg||1
