Z||000047||DaRkLoRD||10-30-2001||06:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>I get "Stevie" occasionally. Depends entirely upon who is saying it, whether it's okay or not.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My sister calls me that sometimes.. and I get "Stevo" sometimes too, but only from people in North Carolina and South Carolina.. nowhere else.. strange.. *twilight music plays quietly in the background*<P>anyway.. just for the record, Cliff's got my support 100% on this, eds had it coming, big time.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000048||fierohoho||10-30-2001||06:50 PM||||Thank you Mr. Pennock.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000049||Cliff Pennock||10-30-2001||06:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>But picture this.. You don't agree with the presidents actions, or you don't vote for him, so you get deported!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I understand your concerns, JohnnyK. But You know as well as I do that I don't ban people because they do not agree with me. I have never done so and probably never will. To be honest, I couldn't care less if people agree with me or not. I will however (eventually) ban people that continue to break the few rules I have set for this forum. True, those are <B>my</B> rules and no democratic process was followed when making those rules, but they are few and IMO not very strict.<P>EdsBS52 has made a total of 3 posts in the TD&Q section and none in the GFC section in the past three months, and all he seemed to be up to lately was stir trouble in the O/T section.<P>I had received <B>a lot</B> of complaints about him through both email and PM. And at some point I have to draw a line. Not for my sake, but for the sake of this forum.<P>Up until 1.5 year ago, PFF was known as that "friendly place" where you could get a lot of good information and where flamewars were far and between. That has changed because a few persons are not able to behave. Now I often read on newsgroups how "unfriendly" this place is. I even read how this place has become my own private dictatorship (...) and how little I tolerate criticism. I've been accused in email of exploiting my role as "Fiero-GOD" (excuse me?). I've been accused of having a hidden commercial agenda. My personal favorite is when I said something like: "I offer this for free and all I ask in return is for the members to follow the few simple rules I've set", and somebody sent me a private email saying: "we've all offered to contribute (financially) so shut up about it or shut down the forum".<P>So really, I don't think I'm being harsh here. Ed is the second person I have banned (or third, if you count the one I had banned, but retracted the ban within an hour) from the forum in all the time the forum has been up. I'm not sure, but I think that makes me quite tolerant. And despite what Ed says, you are <B>not</B> automatically a cheerleader if you agree with what I say or do.<P>But I'm sure he'll be back using a different username/email but probably with the same dictionary under his arm.||||reg||1
Z||000050||Patrick's Dad||10-30-2001||09:35 PM||||My goodness, and I thought the GM Test Drive at Epcot was exciting....<P>My 2¢: The analogy that this is Cliff's house is the right one, which I've said before. A good point was brought earlier that one wouldn't allow this kind of behavior in his or her house; I sure wouldn't. My house is not a democracy, it's a dictatorship. Sometimes it's benevolent, other times not. (My wife just read this. She says it's a actually a monarchy, but that doesn't sound as good....)<P>As for being a cheerleader for Cliff;<P>Rah! Rah! Ree!<BR>Kick 'em in the knee!<BR>Rah! Rah! Rass!<BR>Kick 'em in the other knee!<P>P.S. Wasn't Norm's buddy (on "Cheers") "Cliffie?"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||4
